       "reasons": [
        {
         "@type": "meaningComprehension",
         "comprehends": [
          "copies/dz112ky5575.jsonld#inscription-text"
         ],
         "note": "pencil, four figures run together under the paper edge, both panels agree. The 8 shows two closed bowls, the 1 is a bare slanted stroke, the third figure has the arched top and left-falling diagonal of a 2, and the last is a 4 written as a diagonal, a long crossbar and a stroke descending through it. Read as 8.1.24 with the separators dropped; a four-figure group can also be a roll number, but 8124 lies outside the Welte red numbering, so a date is the only sensible parse."
        }
       ]
      }
     }
    },
